  <constraints>
    <constraint source="§11 reuse">Exactly ONE sanitizer. Writing a second is an automatic code-review failure. If the existing public implementation is unreachable or badly placed, MOVE it and update all callers — never duplicate it.</constraint>
    <constraint source="owner-directive 2026-08-29">Do NOT blanket-sanitize `Api/OBOEndpoints.cs`. Its `{*path}` may legitimately carry separators. Review `ValidatePathForOBO`, harden it, and keep the sub-path capability. Report the finding either way.</constraint>
    <constraint source="owner-directive 2026-08-29">`MessageAttachmentMaterializer.MaterializeAttachmentRequest.DriveId` MUST remain a resolver FALLBACK. If restoring it in any caller-authoritative form appears unavoidable, STOP and report — that is the exact defect class this project exists to close.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-007">All SPE access stays behind the `SpeFileStore` facade. Sanitize at the CALL SITES, not inside the facade — sanitizing in the facade would silently rewrite the OBO route's legitimate sub-paths.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-003">Sanitizing a filename closes the folder-minting half of a site's problems. It does NOT close an authorization hole. Do not let a sanitized `PUT /api/drives/{driveId}/upload` read as fixed — that row is 083's.</constraint>
    <constraint source="tests/CLAUDE.md">Any new ArchTest rule carries BOTH a negative and a positive control, and the positive control must include the real production tree — a synthetic control can pass while the rule flags shipped code.</constraint>
    <constraint source="tests/CLAUDE.md B15">Do NOT write one behavioural test per site. Fourteen mock-heavy tests asserting one string each is the banned setup-to-assertion shape. Blanket site coverage is the source rule's job; behavioural tests cover the distinct MECHANISMS.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Restoring the materializer shifts the sink guard's `(File, Sink, Ordinal)` declarations. Update the declarations. NEVER weaken the rule to make a build green.</constraint>
    <constraint source="CLAUDE.md §10">Placement Justification citing `.claude/constraints/bff-extensions.md`; publish size ≤60 MB (state the five-field convention); `dotnet list package --vulnerable --include-transitive`.</constraint>
    <constraint source="baseline">ArchTests baseline is **6 pre-existing failures** on a clean tree. Prove it with `git stash` before starting; do not assume the number.</constraint>
  </constraints>

